IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `nd-tanf`

-- North Dakota TANF -- the applicant's questions (a parent or caretaker relative, or a pregnant woman). Every question
-- calls the rules in nd-tanf.l4; nothing is restated here.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Can we get TANF`

@export Does the sixty-month limit in N.D.C.C. s 50-09-29(1)(b) stop my household getting TANF?
GIVEN `months of TANF we have had` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months of TANF benefits your household has already had
      `a hardship exemption applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a parent or child has a mental or physical disability, a parent is mentally or physically incapacitated, or there is another hardship such as a parent subject to domestic violence, as determined by the state agency
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the sixty-month limit stop our TANF` IF
    `the sixty-month limit bars benefits` `months of TANF we have had` `a hardship exemption applies`

-- Only if a child is away from the household.
@export A child is away from home: is TANF denied for that child under N.D.C.C. s 50-09-29(1)(s)?
GIVEN `the child has been away more than one calendar month` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the child has been absent from the household for more than one calendar month
      `the agency's absence exception applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the state agency's rules on absences allow this absence (for example a hospital stay)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is TANF denied for the absent child` IF
    `assistance for an absent child is denied` `the child has been away more than one calendar month` `the agency's absence exception applies`

@export Does applying for TANF assign my household's child support rights to the state under N.D.C.C. s 50-09-06.1?
GIVEN `I have applied for TANF` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have made an application for TANF
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does applying assign our support rights` IF
    `the household's support rights are assigned to the state agency` `I have applied for TANF`

§ `Are our savings too high`

@export What is the TANF asset limit for my household under N.D. Admin. Code 75-02-01.2-22?
GIVEN `people in my household` IS A NUMBER @desc How many people are in your TANF household
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is our asset limit` MEANS `the asset limit` `people in my household`

@export Are my household's assets within the TANF asset limit under N.D. Admin. Code 75-02-01.2-22 and N.D.C.C. s 50-09-29(1)(g)?
GIVEN `people in my household` IS A NUMBER @desc How many people are in your TANF household
      `the value of our assets` IS A NUMBER @desc The current market value of your household's assets, in US dollars, not counting one motor vehicle (excluded whatever its value) or individual development account savings
      `the cost of selling them` IS A NUMBER @desc Reasonable costs of turning those assets into cash, in US dollars; 0 if none
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are our assets within the limit` IF
    `the household's assets are within the limit` `people in my household` `the value of our assets` `the cost of selling them`

§ `How much a month`

@export Is the time-limited earned income incentive available to me under N.D. Admin. Code 75-02-01.2-51?
GIVEN `I have had the full twelve months of the incentive` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have already received the full twelve months of the time-limited earned income disregard
      `I have been off TANF twelve months or more since` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, since then, you have been off assistance for twelve or more months
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the earnings incentive available to me` IF
    `the earned income incentive is available` `I have had the full twelve months of the incentive` `I have been off TANF twelve months or more since`

@export How much of my household's monthly earnings counts for TANF under N.D. Admin. Code 75-02-01.2-50 and -51?
GIVEN `monthly gross earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc Gross monthly earnings of the household, in US dollars, leaving out the earnings of a child who is a full-time elementary or high school student
      `the income incentive limit` IS A NUMBER @desc The department's income incentive limit for your household, in US dollars a month
      `month of the incentive` IS A NUMBER @desc Which month this is since your earnings were first budgeted (1 for the first month; 13 or more after twelve months)
      `the incentive is available to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the time-limited earned income incentive is available to you (see the incentive question)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much of our earnings counts` MEANS
    `countable earned income` (`net earned income` `monthly gross earnings`) `the income incentive limit` `month of the incentive` `the incentive is available to me`

@export How much TANF will my household get this month under N.D. Admin. Code 75-02-01.2-47, -48, -42 and -43?
GIVEN `our standard of need` IS A NUMBER @desc The department's TANF standard of need for your household size, in US dollars a month
      `personal needs allowance and special items` IS A NUMBER @desc Any personal needs allowance for a household member living out of the home and special items of need allowed, in US dollars a month; 0 if none
      `our countable earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc Your household's countable earned income (see the earnings question), in US dollars a month
      `our unearned income` IS A NUMBER @desc Unearned income counted for TANF (for example unemployment benefits or child support received), in US dollars a month
      `health insurance premiums and support we pay` IS A NUMBER @desc Health insurance premiums, and child or spousal support you pay, in US dollars a month
      `work-related child care costs` IS A NUMBER @desc Child and dependent care costs you pay so that you can work or train, in US dollars a month
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much TANF a month` MEANS
    `the cash grant` (`adjusted net income` `our countable earnings` `our unearned income` `health insurance premiums and support we pay` `work-related child care costs`) `our standard of need` `personal needs allowance and special items`
